---

Install the pack from [CurseForge](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/modpacks/sc-final-adventure) on NeoForge **1.21.1**. Give the instance **8 GB** if you can. Less works. You will feel it in structure-heavy chunks.

First night is still Minecraft. Punch a tree, make a hole, do not die to something with a title. After that, open FTB Quests. Those chapters are the pack. They are not optional flavor.

Do not race the End. The overworld is full of structures on purpose. Loot and world-tier gear are the actual ladder. Iron’s Spellbooks covers the caster side. Cataclysm and the other bosses are the melee set pieces. You will use both.

When a quest says to go somewhere, go there. When it says to fight something, fight that thing. Skipping ahead just means you show up undergeared and call the pack unfair.

This wiki is the “how the pack wants to be played” notes. Individual mods still have their own pages if you need the HUD or the Codex loop.
